          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How often does water softener resin need to be replaced?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "On chlorine-free water with little iron, resin commonly lasts 10 to 15 years and sometimes 20. On chlorinated city water, standard resin often wears out around year 10, and iron or manganese can foul it within a few years without pre-treatment. Replace it when a correctly set, regenerating softener no longer brings hardness close to zero, or when mushy resin restricts water pressure."
          }
