        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A water softener typically lasts 10 to 15 years, but that number is really the sum of three lifespans. The tanks last decades, the resin lasts as long as your chlorine and iron allow, and the valve lasts as long as you are willing to replace its seals. Know which one is failing before you decide anything.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Protect the resin, keep the salt honest, test the output twice a year, and a well-sized softener can run past 15 years and protect everything downstream. If yours is beyond saving, our <a href="/best-water-softener-system/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-semibold hover:underline">best water softener systems</a> guide will help you size the next one properly.
